WEBVTT

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:06.310
Shoot, Murakoshi!

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:17.330
Keep looking forward.

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:24.960
And above all else, continue developing as a player.

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:26.790
I will not hold back if you break any of these conditions.

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:06.520
C-Conference?

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:09.270
It's the League Press Conference!

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:17.280
All managers from the league will come together and promote their teams to the media.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:20.280
Nah, I'm not cut out for this stuff.

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:23.620
Why are you going back to sleep?!

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:25.410
Get yourself prepared, quick!

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:27.000
We're heading off!

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:40.510
Sorry for the wait!

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:42.760
You guys are slow!

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:45.430
Didn't I tell you to get Tatsumi to dress formally for the event?

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:48.060
I did tell him, but...

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:51.060
It's alright! The enemies' bosses will be swarming this place, right?

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:56.400
Then, this place is going to be a battlefield, meaning that we have to come in our battle suits.

00:02:57.820 --> 00:02:59.110
It's all about our spirit.

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:03.950
Isn't that right, Murakoshi?

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:09.410
The captain looks really smart.

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:14.960
You're dressed really well today, Murakoshi.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:17.840
You are...

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:21.470
Fuwa...

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:24.300
Long time no see, Chairman Nagata.

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:27.970
It's a pleasure to be able to meet you again.

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:31.230
I heard you're now the new manager of Nagoya.

00:03:31.350 --> 00:03:35.110
Be careful there; don't make the same mistakes you made during your reign on our team.

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:38.530
I see you're still the same, shirking your own responsibilities.

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:41.990
No matter how outstanding the manager and his players are...

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:46.240
Their efforts will go to waste if the Board of Directors is not doing its part of the job.

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:48.910
Y-You bastard.

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:53.580
A pleasure to meet you, Tatsumi.

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:58.210
It's going to be a tough job. Do your best.

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:00.340
I'm off then.

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:04.640
Who's that guy?

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:07.560
Fuwa of Nagoya Grand Palace.

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:11.060
He was previously the manager of our club.

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:14.730
He was playing hard ball with the Board of Directors during his reign here...

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:19.280
And we ultimately got relegated to the second division.

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:28.740
And now, let's welcome our Division One's player representatives to our media conference!

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:35.540
Japan League Division One. The player representatives of all 18 teams.

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:39.920
That Murakoshi's holding up his expression really well.

00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:45.220
But I think he looks very intimidating.

00:04:49.060 --> 00:04:52.100
It's my honor to be able to play on the same pitch with you.

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:53.730
I wish the best of luck for both of us.

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:57.860
Thank you. May we have a good match.

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:07.740
Japanese managers are all so polite.

00:05:08.570 --> 00:05:12.790
It will be nice to have a coach that can show a sense of hostility, though...

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:14.870
It can't be helped.

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:22.880
Osaka Gunners, the runner-up for the previous season, scored the most goals.

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:26.760
The leader of their team won't even be able to do so,

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:30.470
Even if he is going up face-to-face with you.

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:49.200
So Tatsumi became a manager here?

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:51.370
Why haven't you contacted us since you came back?

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:53.040
Tatsumi...

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:59.040
I am the translator for Osaka Gunners, Sonoda.

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:01.210
And this person here is...

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:06.970
I am Dulfer, the manager. My best wishes to you.

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:11.930
Hi there! Pleased to meet you.

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:27.240
To all managers, it's about time to make your appearance.

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:28.950
Please prepare yourselves!

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:34.580
Sonoda...

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:35.910
Yes?

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:43.880
He is going to be one hell of a manager.

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:53.300
And so, can we have the defending champion, as well as the Palace Cup winner,

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:57.100
Tokyo Victory's manager, Hirazuimi,

00:06:57.640 --> 00:06:59.600
to talk about his expectations for the season ahead.

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:04.270
During the previous season, we...

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:07.820
The next one will be Tatsumi, I'm kinda worried.

00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:10.990
It'll be alright. I don't think he will do anything foolish.

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:11.490
Our aim is to...
It'll be alright. I don't think he will do anything foolish.

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:11.910
Our aim is to...

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:18.750
Win the league, the Japan Cup, as well as the Palace Cup.

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:23.710
A very ambitious goal from the champions! Thank you for your time.

00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:27.840
The next person will be the returning Star of ETU...

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:30.380
All eyes will be on his managerial abilities this season,

00:07:30.970 --> 00:07:35.050
East Tokyo United's Tatsumi Takeshi, take it away.

00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:39.600
What's that? It's my turn already?

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:42.140
Hey, calm down for a bit!

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:47.690
You guys should be writing something more appropriate. For example, the team's high morale or something.

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:52.240
Well, I've only been a manager for four or five years...

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:55.410
And ETU was only placed 15th last season...

00:07:56.580 --> 00:07:57.660
That's a bit too lousy.

00:07:58.580 --> 00:07:59.870
Can we win it?

00:08:03.210 --> 00:08:07.090
That's good, every one of you will be writing us off...

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:11.010
Which means, for us, this will be the ideal situation to be in.

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:17.680
For the other managers standing here, they will be the ones under pressure to win when they face us.

00:08:18.970 --> 00:08:20.470
If they were to lose to us,

00:08:21.890 --> 00:08:22.940
It would be a huge embarrassment.

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:26.360
We, on the other hand, have nothing to lose.

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:29.440
We will always be in our best condition.

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:35.530
Therefore, for a small and weak club such as ETU, we'll be playing at a higher standard.

00:08:35.870 --> 00:08:40.540
We will then beat these so-called 'big teams' to a pulp. Wouldn't that feel good?

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:47.130
Just wait and see. I will transform the league of this nation into a very exciting one.

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:49.880
That's all.

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:59.930
From what I can see from the pre-season game, ETU should definitely not be underestimated.

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:08.810
Still, you should not naively look down upon this world and do whatever you want, Tatsumi.

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:15.320
Interesting.

00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:21.370
How did this happen? He pushed the limit with his arrogant speech.

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:23.500
Are you okay, Yuri?

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:31.210
Mr. Tatsumi?

00:09:32.590 --> 00:09:37.640
I would like to have a word with you. Would you join me for lunch?

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:41.810
Who are you?

00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:46.640
I am a football manager, just like you.

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:54.860
Do you like Fish & Chips?

00:09:56.570 --> 00:10:00.410
I am a Frenchman, but I used to manage a team in England.

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:04.700
Back then, I had it almost every day.

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:10.960
I know a place nearby, where they serve good and cheap Fish & Chips.

00:10:11.420 --> 00:10:12.630
Let's go.

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:19.590
That's weird, where did Tatsumi go?

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:23.560
Don't tell me... he ran off?

00:10:27.230 --> 00:10:31.520
Hey old man, you said you are a manager, so which team are you managing?

00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:34.730
You look familiar somehow.

00:10:37.650 --> 00:10:38.820
Monsieur Tatsumi...

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:41.320
Listen.

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:44.990
I don't want you to panic or anything,

00:10:45.410 --> 00:10:46.660
But I think,

00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:48.460
We are lost.

00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:50.670
We're lost?!

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:53.960
And you were the one told me to follow you, right?

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:02.050
Here, my recommended lunch set.

00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:06.520
It looks like, I've put you through a lot of trouble...

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:09.270
For nothing, dear me.

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:13.360
It's fine. Besides, I get to escape from that troublesome conference.

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:22.110
Go!

00:11:24.740 --> 00:11:25.660
The ball's there!

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:35.920
Which side do you think will win?

00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:37.920
The blue team.

00:11:38.710 --> 00:11:40.760
But they're behind.

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:43.760
They will turn the game around soon.

00:11:44.090 --> 00:11:48.060
Because they are running more emphatically than the red team.

00:11:49.430 --> 00:11:55.770
What's more, they look more spirited. These kind of players are tough to beat.

00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:58.690
That's true for the pros as well.

00:12:03.110 --> 00:12:06.830
Is that the kind of football you're aiming for?

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:10.830
If so, we share the same view.

00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:18.460
You know, they should have opened up the side a little more..

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:22.840
They should have do it just like <i>this</i> here, and do it just like <i>that</i> there.

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:25.300
Yeah, yeah! Just like this and that!

00:12:26.180 --> 00:12:27.010
Also, don't forget this!

00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:33.100
Where did he run off to? He shouldn't have gone far...

00:12:38.980 --> 00:12:39.980
There you are!

00:12:41.650 --> 00:12:42.740
Hey, that guy's...

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:47.950
He's that French guy!

00:12:49.240 --> 00:12:52.500
Japan National Team's manager, Blanc?!

00:12:53.660 --> 00:12:57.330
What is this? Why is he together with him?

00:12:58.340 --> 00:13:01.340
And they are happily chatting away.

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:04.430
As if they are friends...

00:13:08.430 --> 00:13:09.720
We won!

00:13:14.850 --> 00:13:16.650
Good luck with your season.

00:13:17.650 --> 00:13:21.150
I'm sure you'll put together a fine team.

00:13:22.070 --> 00:13:25.320
I won't know that until I've tried it.

00:13:25.900 --> 00:13:27.700
Of course you can!

00:13:28.530 --> 00:13:30.450
You have the luck!

00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:34.660
Luck, huh?

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:36.540
I think so.

00:13:38.290 --> 00:13:42.960
Besides, I have yet to pay my debt back to the footballing god.

00:13:47.470 --> 00:13:48.550
I found you!

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:53.470
I've been searching for you, Monsieur Blanc.

00:13:53.560 --> 00:13:55.060
I'm sorry.

00:13:55.600 --> 00:13:59.520
Didn't I tell you that you'll be having dinner with the people of the Association?

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:01.520
Ahh, yes.

00:14:03.980 --> 00:14:05.150
You got caught!

00:14:05.610 --> 00:14:06.950
That's not good, old man.

00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:09.240
How can you do such a thing?

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:12.240
That's right!

00:14:12.740 --> 00:14:14.950
So you know that too!

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:23.000
The next time we meet, we'll have Fish & Chips!

00:14:26.170 --> 00:14:27.010
Later.

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:36.980
Monsieur Blanc, you're putting us in a tight spot with your actions.

00:14:37.640 --> 00:14:40.600
Please know your limits, sir. The whole of Japan is putting their hopes on you.

00:14:41.810 --> 00:14:44.070
Cheer up a little bit.

00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:45.360
What?

00:14:46.900 --> 00:14:53.160
Today's little incident will have a great positive impact to the Japanese National Team.

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:06.420
Alright! I've remembered them all!

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:07.800
Come on!

00:15:08.170 --> 00:15:12.220
Is the No.2 Kuroda single, or married?

00:15:12.850 --> 00:15:13.470
Single.

00:15:13.720 --> 00:15:17.520
Correct! Then, what is Gino's favorite car?

00:15:22.310 --> 00:15:24.270
Time's up!

00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:30.950
No good. Tomorrow's the opening game!

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:39.370
The Japan National Team will definitely pick out players from ETU!

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:42.460
Yuri, you've been repeating that several times.

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:47.630
That's because I saw Tatsumi and Manager Blanc chatting away happily!

00:15:48.130 --> 00:15:51.970
Well, the two of them <i>are</i> weird. They should click right away.

00:15:52.260 --> 00:15:56.810
There will certainly be more surprises in store for the ETU.

00:15:57.850 --> 00:16:02.140
That's why we have to make preparations for this season's opener! Let's do our best!

00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:03.100
That's right.

00:16:10.030 --> 00:16:12.490
Matsubara and the rest are still here?

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:15.370
The coaching staff had a meeting just now.

00:16:16.280 --> 00:16:20.700
We've decided to come together to mould Tatsumi into an important figure of our team!

00:16:21.790 --> 00:16:24.330
Alright! We're going to rile up the pre-match atmosphere!

00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:29.960
And so, they are starting it off with their usual drinking sessions.

00:16:30.590 --> 00:16:33.630
Yuri, Tatsumi is still...

00:16:36.010 --> 00:16:39.810
He's still cooped up in his room... Is he planning to not come out?

00:16:44.270 --> 00:16:45.810
Ok, a little bit more...

00:16:46.730 --> 00:16:48.270
Don't drag our time.

00:16:51.190 --> 00:16:54.910
Tomorrow's the day... We've made it.

00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:59.330
With this, the season opener is going to be a riot.

00:17:00.040 --> 00:17:02.120
I'm already all psyched up!

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:05.540
What do you think of the ETU team this season, Haneda?

00:17:06.420 --> 00:17:09.380
Stripping Murakoshi of his captaincy initially, and then renominating him again...

00:17:10.050 --> 00:17:13.050
I'm not really satisfied with the way Tatsumi does things, to be honest.

00:17:14.130 --> 00:17:18.970
Besides, he did abandon ETU in the past. I do not approve of Tatsumi's appointment...

00:17:20.310 --> 00:17:25.730
But we are the United Skulls. We're formed to bring ETU victory.

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:28.110
We need to believe in our own powers.

00:17:28.900 --> 00:17:31.020
The ones that will strengthen the team up is us, the fans!

00:17:57.840 --> 00:18:00.010
Paoka, shake my hand!

00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:02.260
Me too, me too!

00:18:03.850 --> 00:18:05.680
Ignoring the guys, are you?!

00:18:09.020 --> 00:18:12.650
Sumidagawa stadium... Though I haven't come for a long time,

00:18:13.730 --> 00:18:15.490
This place is still so small and narrow.

00:18:16.030 --> 00:18:17.650
Oh? Miss Fujii!

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:21.580
This is a rare sight. What brings you here?

00:18:21.700 --> 00:18:22.660
Mr Yamai.

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:27.250
I'm planning to be reporting exclusively on ETU for this season.

00:18:28.170 --> 00:18:32.420
It will be a great help if you are able to help me in the exclusive reports, since ETU's your specialty.

00:18:33.210 --> 00:18:36.380
As long as it's for you, I'll do all I can to help.

00:18:37.590 --> 00:18:41.220
It is definitely not easy for freelance reporters like you to be able to get reports on Tokyo Victory.

00:18:42.350 --> 00:18:45.390
Besides, reports for the top teams are all written by top reporters from the press.

00:18:45.770 --> 00:18:47.930
The boss made the right choice of getting you for this job.

00:18:47.980 --> 00:18:48.600
Later then.

00:18:54.520 --> 00:18:58.280
Transforming the league of this nation into an exciting one?

00:19:00.110 --> 00:19:03.580
Show me what you've got then, Tatsumi Takeshi.

00:19:12.750 --> 00:19:13.540
Let's go.

00:19:18.720 --> 00:19:20.340
Alright, they're out!

00:19:21.050 --> 00:19:23.350
Open your eyes wide and look over here!

00:19:23.850 --> 00:19:28.560
These are the fans that will be going through thick and thin with you this season!

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:49.000
What a great job from the Skulls!

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:52.620
This is going to make publicity stunts so much easier.

00:19:55.290 --> 00:20:00.130
The fans are brimming with so much passion... it feels just like a rowdy summer vacation back in Italy.

00:20:00.130 --> 00:20:02.590
What exactly is this "summer vacation in Italy"?

00:20:03.970 --> 00:20:07.890
The atmosphere is huge! We're only playing against Iwata, there's nothing to fear!

00:20:07.890 --> 00:20:10.430
You're noisy, so stop wasting your breath, Kuro.

00:20:12.480 --> 00:20:13.600
Tatsumi Takeshi.

00:20:14.560 --> 00:20:17.150
During the friendly against Tokyo Victory as well as the media conference,

00:20:18.480 --> 00:20:22.610
He possesses a certain quality that captures people's attention.

00:20:23.860 --> 00:20:30.040
My hopes are on you. I'm putting my entire freelance career on your shoulders.

00:20:32.750 --> 00:20:36.080
The opponent today is Javelin Iwata, which finished 6th in the previous season.

00:20:36.540 --> 00:20:38.090
Leading the team for fourteen years...

00:20:39.000 --> 00:20:43.720
Kurashi has built up a team which emphasizes passing. He's sly rather than smart.

00:20:45.930 --> 00:20:50.680
Time flies, doesn't it? The kid from before has now become a manager.

00:20:51.220 --> 00:20:55.440
And when exactly was that, old man? It's still too early for you to go senile, you know.

00:20:55.810 --> 00:21:00.820
The society's getting older, learn to have some manners.

00:21:01.490 --> 00:21:02.780
I'm not really into that sort of thing.

00:21:08.950 --> 00:21:11.450
Tsk, that old hag.

00:21:12.750 --> 00:21:15.580
I'd hoped to meet him much later...

00:21:17.290 --> 00:21:21.920
I'm not letting you do what you did when you faced Tokyo Victory, Tatsumi.

00:21:22.960 --> 00:21:26.800
I am definitely a much more crafty opponent than Hirazumi.

00:21:30.640 --> 00:21:33.480
The captain of ETU is still Murakoshi.

00:21:33.980 --> 00:21:36.520
ETU is still the same old squad.

00:21:37.650 --> 00:21:39.360
The majority still thinks of it that way.

00:21:41.270 --> 00:21:42.780
However, we'll show them.

00:21:46.240 --> 00:21:48.320
We have to win and prove a point!

00:22:07.680 --> 00:22:08.300
That was close!

00:22:08.430 --> 00:22:09.180
Continue the attack!

00:22:09.890 --> 00:22:12.350
Not bad! We should be able to score first!

00:22:14.430 --> 00:22:19.100
It's for real. The quality we displayed previously against Tokyo Victory is for real.

00:22:20.560 --> 00:22:22.320
I'm sorry, Prince! I'll get it the next time!

00:22:23.230 --> 00:22:26.950
It's up to you, Sera. That was a great chance just now.

00:22:27.780 --> 00:22:29.950
That's right, we can do it!

00:22:31.490 --> 00:22:34.290
What's up with these guys? They're closing up so tightly!

00:22:37.580 --> 00:22:42.840
Even the dead ball specialist, Tanabe, is forced into making errors. The game is slowly turning in our favour.

00:24:17.260 --> 00:24:17.890
Pass it!

00:24:18.100 --> 00:24:18.560
Quick!

00:24:19.810 --> 00:24:21.390
Stop your aimless running, Tsubaki!

00:24:23.600 --> 00:24:25.860
Stop joking, you bastard!

00:24:26.940 --> 00:24:28.360
A competition?!
